/T (5.1  The Engagement Letter contains a description of the Work to be performed by MAC.  5.2  MAC will exert itself to the best of its abilities to perform the Work in accordance with the arrangements and procedures agreed in writing with the Client.  5.3  MAC will determine how and by which person or persons the Work will be performed. If the Engagement Letter provides that specifically named persons will perform the Work, MAC will make reasonable efforts to ensure that these persons perform the Work. MAC has the right to replace the persons named in the Engagement Letter by persons of equal or comparable expertise.   5.4  If a phased performance of the Work has been agreed, MAC may postpone commencing Work relating to a subsequent phase until the Client has accepted the results of the preceding phase in writing and has paid all sums due.  5.5  Time-limits within which the Work must be completed will not be considered as strict deadlines, unless this has been expressly agreed. Under no circumstances may the Client dissolve the Agreement on account of a failure to meet a time-limit. Furthermore, MAC will never be liable for compensation on account of any failure to meet a time-limit.  5.6  If, at the request or with the prior consent of the Client, MAC carries out work or performs outside the content or scope of the Work, the Client will pay MAC for such work or performance on the basis of MAC's customary rates. )
/E (5.1  The Engagement Letter contains a description of the Work to be performed by MAC.  5.2  MAC will exert itself to the best of its abilities to perform the Work in accordance with the arrangements and procedures agreed in writing with the Client.  5.3  MAC will determine how and by which person or persons the Work will be performed. If the Engagement Letter provides that specifically named persons will perform the Work, MAC will make reasonable efforts to ensure that these persons perform the Work. MAC has the right to replace the persons named in the Engagement Letter by persons of equal or comparable expertise.   5.4  If a phased performance of the Work has been agreed, MAC may postpone commencing Work relating to a subsequent phase until the Client has accepted the results of the preceding phase in writing and has paid all sums due.  5.5  Time-limits within which the Work must be completed will not be considered as strict deadlines, unless this has been expressly agreed. Under no circumstances may the Client dissolve the Agreement on account of a failure to meet a time-limit. Furthermore, MAC will never be liable for compensation on account of any failure to meet a time-limit.  5.6  If, at the request or with the prior consent of the Client, MAC carries out work or performs outside the content or scope of the Work, the Client will pay MAC for such work or performance on the basis of MAC's customary rates. )
