/Title (5.1  The Engagement Letter contains a description of the Work to be performed by MAC.  5.2  MAC will exert itself to the best of its abilities to perform the Work in accordance with the arrangements and procedures agreed in writing with the Client.  5.3  MAC will determine how and by which person or persons the Work will be performed. If the Engagement Letter provides that specifically named persons will perform the Work, MAC will make reasonable efforts to ensure that these persons perform the Work. MAC has the right to replace the persons named in the Engagement Letter by persons of equal or comparable expertise.   5.4  If a phased performance of the Work has been agreed, MAC may postpone commencing Work relating to a subsequent phase until the Client has accepted the results of the preceding phase in writing and has paid all sums due.  5.5  Time-limits within which the Work must be completed will not be considered as strict deadlines, unless this has been expressly agreed. Under no circumstances may the Client dissolve the Agreement on account of a failure to meet a time-limit. Furthermore, MAC will never be liable for compensation on account of any failure to meet a time-limit.  5.6  If, at the request or with the prior consent of the Client, MAC carries out work or performs outside the content or scope of the Work, the Client will pay MAC for such work or performance on the basis of MAC's customary rates.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 951 0 R
>>
endobj
1103 0 obj
<<
/Title (6.1  Both of its own accord and at the request of MAC, the Client will give its full cooperation and will in good time and in the desired form and manner make available all relevant documents which MAC may reasonably deem necessary to receive from the Client for the proper performance of the Work. If MAC works at the Client's premises or makes use of the Client's computer systems and telephone networks, the Client will \(at its own expense\) provide the necessary access, security procedures, virus controls, facilities, licenses and permissions. If any part of the Work is not performed at MAC's own premises, the Client will also ensure that the employees of MAC are provided with adequate working space and other facilities necessary for the performance of the Work, which should meet all the applicable statutory or other requirements.  6.2 The Client will ensure that MAC is informed without delay of facts and circumstances which may be relevant in connection with the proper performance of the Work.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 954 0 R
>>
endobj
