/Title (8.2  The obligation of paragraph 1 of this Article does not apply if the information referred to in that paragraph becomes publicly known. Furthermore, this obligation is without prejudice to the right of MAC to submit information referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article to its insurers and/or advisers in connection with MAC's professional liability or to a MAC Member Firm if this is necessary for the support of its services.  8.3  MAC is not authorized to use the information which the Client has placed at its disposal for another purpose than that for which it was obtained, unless MAC acts for itself, or persons employed by or for or attached to MAC act for themselves, in disciplinary, criminal or civil proceedings in which this information may be relevant.  8.4  Unless the Client has obtained prior written permission from MAC, the Client will not disclose the content of the Engagement Letter, reports, advice or other statements made by MAC, whether or not in writing, which were not prepared or made for the purpose of providing the information contained therein to third parties. The Client will, moreover, ensure that third parties cannot take note of the content referred to in the preceding sentence.  8.5  Except with prior written permission from MAC, the Client will not make any statements about the approach and working procedures used by MAC.  8.6  The Client may exclusively use the quotation made by MAC and the knowledge and ideas of MAC contained in this quotation for the purposes of evaluating its interest in awarding the engagement.  8.7  MAC and the Client will impose their obligations pursuant to Article 8 on third parties engaged by them.  8.8  MAC reserves the right to use the Client's name and to mention the kind of work it performed for the Client for publicity and reference purposes, and to mention all particulars which have already been made publicly known in the media.)
