/Title (11.4  The amount invoiced by MAC may differ from earlier estimates or quotations.  11.5  Invoices will be paid by the Client, without any deduction, subject to TDS deduction, discount or setoff, within 15 days of the invoice date. If the Client fails to pay an invoice within this payment period, MAC will be entitled, without further notice of default and without prejudice to the other rights of MAC, to charge the Client legal commercial interest from the due date until the date of payment in full.  11.6  All judicial and extrajudicial collection and other costs reasonably incurred by MAC as a result of the Client's failure to discharge its payment obligations will be borne by the Client.  11.7  If, in the opinion of MAC, the Client's financial position or payment record gives reason to do so, MAC may require the Client to make a full or partial advance payment and/or to provide \(additional\) security in a form to be determined by MAC. If the Client fails to provide the required security, MAC may, without prejudice to its other rights, immediately suspend the further performance of the Agreement and any amounts owing by the Client to MAC on any account whatsoever will be immediately due and payable.  11.8  If several Clients have jointly awarded an engagement, the Clients will be jointly and severally liable for payment of the invoice amount to the extent that the Work was performed for the Clients jointly.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1107 0 R
