/Title (16.1  In performing the Work or in complying with its statutory obligations, MAC may process personal data concerning the Client and/or persons associated with or employed by or for the Client. 16.2  MAC may process personal data for the purposes of supporting MAC's services to the Client and to enable MAC to approach the Client and/or persons employed by or for the Client with information and with services provided by MAC and third parties, including other MAC Member Firms. 16.3  MAC will process personal data in carrying out the activities mentioned in paragraphs 1 and 2 in accordance with the applicable legislation and regulations in the field of personal data protection.)
